          "_label": "Details (Official List Description)"
        }
      ],
      "content": "SP 90 SW              THE LEE              FIELD END LANE                                            (south side)   5/99                                       Hawthorn Farmhouse - -                                          II Farmhouse.  Dated 1740.  Flint brick dressings, north elevation roughcast, south-east wing brick, old tile roof.  Three bay main range, centre bay gabled and projecting.  Later C18 south east wing of one bay.  C19 infill to south west.  Two storeys with half-hipped attics to south wings. Sashes and casements.  1740 block with moulded brick eaves and parapet, copings to east gable, band course and window jambs and arches.  Brick date panel in east gable 'WHM 1740'. Manor Lodge in a modern house attached to the west end of the farmhouse and is of no historic interest. Listing NGR: SP9005304224"
    }
  ],
